# Making fishing easier or harder

Open `/poggy`, pick **Poggy Fishing**, then one of these tabs:

- **The bite & fight**: the wait for a bite, the tug game and the skillcheck rules.
- **Difficulty tiers**: one section per tier, with its skillchecks, tug game scaling and Pro Rod drain.
- **Pro Rod**: the mouse-driven pull fight.

Every change needs a restart of the script.

## Price sets the tier

A fish's price decides how hard it is.

| Price | Tier |
|---|---|
| under $1 | Easy |
| $1 to $2.99 | Medium |
| $3 to $5.99 | Hard |
| $6 to $19.99 | Expert |
| $20 or more | Legendary |

Raising a fish's price in the **Fish** list (Baits & fish tab) can move it to a harder tier.

## The tug game (normal rod)

- Want fewer taps? Raise **Starting interest** or **Interest per tap**.
- Line snapping too often? Lower **Tension per tap** or raise **Tension lost per second**.
- Fish leaving too soon? Raise **Boredom timeout** or **Grace period**.

Each tier scales these values. The scaling is on the **Difficulty tiers** tab, under **Show advanced**.

## The fight (both rods)

Each tier has its own skillcheck settings on the **Difficulty tiers** tab.

- **Progress per good hit** sets how long a fight lasts. The fish lands at 100.
  12 means about nine hits.
- **Zone difficulty** 1 is a big zone, 5 is a small one.
- **Needle speed** 1 is slow, 5 is very fast.
- **Off-centre scatter** (under **Show advanced**): keep it at 2 or lower, or checks can hide behind the HUD.
- **Misses before the line breaks** only applies to the normal rod.

## The Pro Rod

- **Progress drain** is how fast the fish pulls line back. Lower it to make fights easier.
- **Pro Rod drain ×** in each tier (Difficulty tiers tab) makes big fish pull harder.
- **Tension gain when wrong** and **Tension spike on a miss** decide how fast the line snaps.
- **Mouse sensitivity** changes how twitchy the pull needle feels.

## Quick recipes

| Goal | Change |
|---|---|
| Shorter fights | Raise **Progress per good hit** on each tier |
| Fewer escapes on the Pro Rod | Lower **Progress drain** |
| More legendary fish | Raise the Pro Rod's **Legendary fish ×** |
| Every fish always in season | Set **Fish in season** to 100 |
